---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Brief = `Build me a working traffic light. Red, then green, then
amber, then round again, on its own, at a sensible speed.`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/unit-1/cc-set-2" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back to Set 2
        </a>

        <h1>Code Challenge: Traffic Light</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="brief">
          <h2>The Brief</h2>

          <Code
            code={Brief}
            frame="code"
            lang="txt"
            title="What they asked for"
            showLineNumbers={false}
            class="mt-3"
          />

          <p class="mt-4">
            <b>Write your requirements list before you write any code.</b> What
            the player does, what happens on screen, and{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">every question the brief did not
            answer.</b>
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="notes">
          <h2>Notes</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>You drew this at session 2. Now one of the three is lit and the other two are dark.</li>
            <li><b>Something has to remember which light is on</b>, and something has to count time. Both live above <code>love.draw</code>.</li>
            <li>A timer is a variable that <code>dt</code> is added to. When it passes a threshold, act and reset it &mdash; <b>reset it, do not set it to zero and forget</b>.</li>
            <li>Amber is shorter than the other two. The brief does not say how much. Decide.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="success">
          <h2>What Success Looks Like</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>The three lights cycle on their own with no key presses</li>
            <li>Exactly one is lit at any moment</li>
            <li>The cycle repeats forever without drifting or sticking</li>
            <li>Changing one variable changes how fast the whole thing runs</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="mt-3"><b>Test it by leaving it running for two minutes.</b> A timer that is reset wrongly drifts, and two minutes is enough to see it.</p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Your requirements list and your program folder, named{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">cc-traffic-light</b>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Challenge
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
